<https://hexplain.io/ns/register/checksum#CRC16> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE integrity check: polynomial 0x1021, initial value 0xFFFF, no input or output reflection and final XOR 0x0000 (check value 0x29B1 over the ASCII bytes 123456789). Other CRC-16 variants, such as CRC-16/ARC or CRC-16/XMODEM, are not identified by this term; identifiers for them are future work."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/register/checksum#CRC16> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use as a controlled value or grouping in this register. Profiles bind the appropriate scheme and map their raw wire codes to concept IRIs; membership does not prescribe a wire code. Codec/algorithm concepts require any applicable variant, framing and parameter information from the profile."@en .
